   "date": "2014-11-07T16:28:47Z",
   "subject": "How to update a reactiveValues object?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Hello everybody!</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br></p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">I have a pair of auxiliary inputs that allows user to choose combinations from a set of choices. Also, it is convenient one to be able to remove an item that was created before.</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">For this task, a named list, in the form of reactiveValues object, <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13.3333339691162px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background:rgb(238,238,238)\">listN &lt;- reactiveValues()</code>, will be in charge to store these information.</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">The function to ADD items is working like a charm, but when I try to REMOVE items from <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13.3333339691162px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background:rgb(238,238,238)\">listN</code>, its item names persists forever!</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">My strategy was make use of <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13.3333339691162px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background:rgb(238,238,238)\">reactiveValuesToList()</code>, manipulate its items and replace <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13.3333339691162px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background:rgb(238,238,238)\">listN</code> with a brand new instance of <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13.3333339691162px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background:rgb(238,238,238)\">reactiveValues()</code> (or <code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13.3333339691162px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background:rgb(238,238,238)\">do.call(reactiveValues, listN_as_list)</code>.</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">I stored a reproducible app at Gist. I hope it is sufficient to you guys help me out. Please insist in more clarification if needed.</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">URL:</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><a href=\"http://gist.github.com/d43e72959c4576d27535\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;color:rgb(74,107,130);background:transparent\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gist.github.com/d43e72959c4576d27535&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792396435593000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3jxUOoYdvxCGmlnb40TBns\">gist.github.com/d43e72959c4576d27535</a></p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Code to run on console:</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><code style=\"padding:1px 5px;font-size:13.3333339691162px;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;white-space:pre-wrap;background:rgb(238,238,238)\">shiny::runGist(&#39;d43e72959c4576d27535&#39;)</code></p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">Thanks in advance!</p><p style=\"font-size:13.3333339691162px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif;line-height:17.804801940918px;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\">PS: Shiny is an awesome feature, congratulations and thank you!</p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "KD6sMS-mtFUJ",
   "from": "Joe Cheng",
   "author": "ca443e6eaa0e78ed",
   "date": "2014-11-07T17:14:01Z",
   "subject": "Re: How to update a reactiveValues object?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Yeah, you can&#39;t replace an entire reactiveValues instance like that and expect anything that&#39;s bound to the previous reactiveValues instance to instantly know about the new one. The slots on the reactiveValues instance itself are reactive, but its own variable is not.<div><br></div><div>I think the real issue here is that, unlike lists and envs, you can&#39;t remove values from reactiveValues, only set them to NULL.</div><div><br></div><div>There are two easy workarounds I can think of:</div><div><ol><li>In addition to the reactiveValues instance&#39;s slots being reactive, also make the variable reactive, using makeReactiveBinding.</li><li>You could also use reactiveValues as normal, but keep a list IN the reactiveValues that holds the combinations, not having the reactiveValues itself hold the values. In other words, values &lt;- reactiveValues(combos = list()), and when something new gets added, values$combos[[x]] &lt;- y.</li></ol><div>In trying out fix #1 above, I found that updateSelectInput doesn&#39;t work properly when choices is a length-0 vector. Instead of sending a 0-length vector to the client, it doesn&#39;t send anything for choices at all, so the choices never change.</div></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve forked your gist and added two revisions: one that implements workaround #1 (along with some other problems I found), and one that works around the updateSelectInput issue by using renderUI.</div><div><a href=\"https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/eaedfed5095d37217fca/revisions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/eaedfed5095d37217fca/revisions&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792396435596000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1cHQnW1qS--8k7dSe224Cr\">https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/eaedfed5095d37217fca/revisions</a><br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Nov 7, 2014 at 8:28 AM, Athos Damiani <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">athos....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
